== Leveling ==
* Players can tier up their {{HotM}} by gaining {{HotM EXP}}, which can be accumulated by: 
** completing [[Commissions]]: {{See also|Commissions}}
*** from the {{zone|Dwarven Mines}}, each rewarding {{HotM EXP|+100}} at '''HotM Level''' {{Green|1}}, {{HotM EXP|+200}} at '''HotM Level {{Green|2}}''' and {{HotM EXP|+400}} at '''HotM Level {{Green|3}}''' and above;
*** from the {{zone|Crystal Hollows}}, each rewarding {{HotM EXP|+400}}.
*** from the {{zone|Glacite Tunnels}}, each rewarding {{HotM EXP|+750}}.
*** The first {{Green|4}} daily [[Commissions]] award an additional {{HotM EXP|+900}}. At '''HotM Level''' {{Green|10}}, this bonus is replaced with {{Mithril Powder|1,600}}, {{Gemstone Powder|3,200}} or {{Glacite Powder|4,000}}, depending on the area.
** participating in various active [[Mining Events]]. {{See also|Mining Events}}
** completing {{zone|Crystal Nucleus}} Runs, each rewarding {{HotM EXP|+800}}. {{See also|Nucleus Runs}}
*{{HotM EXP}} gains from [[Commissions]] can be increased by {{green|1%}}→{{green|10%}} from the {{Attribute|Mountain Climber}} attribute ({{Item|Troglobyte Shard}}).
*All {{HotM EXP}} can be increased by  {{green|1%}}→{{green|10%}} from the {{Attribute|Dwarven Training}} attribute ({{Item|Treasure Hoarder Shard}}).
* The {{HotM}} can be reset. This reverts all perk purchases and reimburses all spent {{Mithril Powder}}, {{Gemstone Powder}}, {{Glacite Powder}} and [[Token of the Mountain|{{DarkPurple|Tokens of the Mountain}}]]. 
** Tier and Core of the Mountain levels are kept; thus powder spent on upgrading Core of the Mountain is not reimbursed.

